        "id": 5046
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-01-11T20:45:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It would be nice if we could use jsonschema\u0027s built-in support for date-time validation[0]. The thing is that it has a dependency on strict-rfc3339 [1], which is GPL licensed :( \n\nI am on board with Tin\u0027s approach towards finding something to do this validation for us instead of having to maintain an test our own regular expression. Exploring timeutils sounds like a good idea.\n\n[0] https://python-jsonschema.readthedocs.io/en/latest/validate/#validating-formats\n\n[1] https://pypi.python.org/pypi/strict-rfc3339/",
      "parentUuid": "ba5201f7_76881d72",
      "revId": "06ef92126debd9d4c330890f1abae15e32bdcd4c",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
